# Author: Oleksii Hnidan
# Project: web-security26 | Lab: 2 | File: tracks.http
# Run the requests from top to bottom against the application on localhost:8080.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080/api/v1/tracks

### 1. Get all tracks
GET {{baseUrl}}
Accept: application/json

### 2. Get one track
GET {{baseUrl}}/1
Accept: application/json

### 3. Create a track (the in-memory service assigns id 4)
POST {{baseUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "title": "Be Quiet and Drive (Far Away)",
  "artist": "Deftones",
  "album": "Around the Fur",
  "durationSeconds": 300
}

### 4. Update the created track
PUT {{baseUrl}}/4
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "title": "Be Quiet and Drive (Far Away)",
  "artist": "Deftones",
  "album": "Around the Fur",
  "durationSeconds": 301
}

### 5. Delete the created track
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/4
Accept: application/json
